/-!
# Fixed finite tables for the quotient census

The tables select actual Q elements from the checked multiplication program.
The commuting-subgroup tables have 640, 2688, and 2304 proposed distinct
entries. The proposed Sylow table has 256 entries. Their sizes, subgroup
properties, and fusion conditions require separate finite certificates;
these definitions do not assert the results of the discovery computation.
See `source/README.md` for bit, word, and conjugation conventions.
-/

